AN AMENDED ORDINANCE TO PROVIDE FOR THE ISSUANCE OF RETAIL BEER AND WINE SALES LICENSES WITHIN THE UNINCORPORATED AREAS OF TREUTLEN COUNTY, GEORGIA.

On this day, the 1st day of November, 2011, the Treutlen County Board of Commissioners have met for the purpose of discussing and passing an amendment to the existing Treutlen County Beer Ordinance, as originally passed on February 15, 1978, so as to allow license holders to sell both beer and wine;

WHEREAS said Treutlen County Beer Ordinance: had previously been amended on several occasions, that being February 7, 1984, September 6, 1994, and April 3, 2007; and

WHEREAS, the Treutlen County Board of Commissioners believes that it is necessary to amend the existing Treutlen County Beer Ordinance, previously enacted, in order to provide for and authorize the sale of wine and to specify and otherwise clarify the rules and regulations concerning the issuance of licenses and the operation of licensed premises;

WHEREFORE, upon a motion and second by the Treutlen County Commissioners, the Treutlen County Board of Commissioners have hereunto passed and enacted the following amendment to said ordinance, to be known now as the “Treutlen County Beer and Wine License Ordinance”:

Said Ordinance shall hereafter read as follows:

It is ordained by the Commissioners of Treutlen County, Georgia, as follows:

WHEREAS, consistent with Georgia Law, the Treutlen County Board of Commissioners has the authority to establish by ordinance or resolution such local rules and regulations, not in conflict with existing State or Federal Law, relating to the health, safety, and welfare of the public;

BE IN NOW RESOLVED that the following rules and regulations regarding the sale of beer and wine are hereby adopted. These regulations shall apply to all unincorporated land located within the boundaries of Treutlen County, Georgia.

9:
No licensee shall sell or offer for sale any alcoholic beverage at any of the following times:

- (1) At any time on Sunday;

- (2) At any time in violation of a local ordinance or regulation of a special order of the Treutlen County Board of Commissioners;

- (3) On Monday through Saturday after 12:00 midnight or before 8:00 a.m.; (4) At any time on Christmas Day.

- (5) On any election day, until such time as all local polling stations close, as set forth by applicable law.

- (6) At any other time or day as may be prohibited or regulated by applicable Georgia law.

20:
- (a) No beer or wine license shall be granted to any person unless the entire business premises of the proposed location is situated beyond five hundred (500’) feet from any church and beyond five hundred (500’) feet from any school ground or college campus, distances to be measured by the most direct route of travel on the ground and shall be measured in the following manner:

- (1) From the front door of the structure from which beer and wine are sold or offered for sale;

- (2) Ina straight line to the nearest public sidewalk, walkway, street, road or highway;

- (3) Along such public sidewalk, walkway, street, road or highway by the nearest route;

- (4) To the front door of the building, or to the nearest portion of the grounds, whichever is applicable under the appropriate statute.

- (b) Each application for a license shall include a scale drawing of the location of the proposed premises showing the distance to the nearest church or school or a certificate of a registered surveyor that such location complies with this article with reference to this section.

